message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Rheome: a MATLAB toolbox for the multiscale geometry of human cortical dynamics"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
date-released: 2026-10-08
authors:
  - family-names: Basha
    given-names: Diellor
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9312-8633"
    affiliation: "McGill University; Centre de recherche du CHUM (CRCHUM), Université de Montréal"
  - family-names: Baillet
    given-names: Sylvain
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6762-5713"
    affiliation: "Université de Montréal; Centre de recherche du CHUM (CRCHUM); McGill University"
repository-code: "https://github.com/neurodynamics-xr/rheome"
url: "https://github.com/neurodynamics-xr/rheome"
abstract: >-
  Rheome is a MATLAB toolbox for the multiscale geometry of human cortical dynamics: spatiotemporal
  dynamics on graphs -- cortical meshes, connectomes and sensor arrays. Graph wavelet frames
  (rheome.graphfilterbank, rheome.jointfilterbank, rheome.timefilterbank) modelled on MATLAB's
  cwtfilterbank, the joint (lambda, omega) plane, phase geometry, and cortical flow (divergence,
  rotation, Helmholtz-Hodge, surface optical flow) from MEG source estimates.
keywords:
  - MEG
  - cortical dynamics
  - cortical flow
  - graph signal processing
  - graph wavelets
  - Laplace-Beltrami
  - Helmholtz-Hodge decomposition
  - MATLAB
